session:pr722Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #694 was the one OWL/XML axiom element left unhandled after #605-#608's dispatch coverage: <DatatypeDefinition>. Read owl_xml_parser's existing axiom.rs (#606, class axioms) and property_axiom.rs (#607, property axioms/HasKey) to confirm the established per-crate conventions before writing anything: element_children() helper, an up-front check for an axiom-level <Annotation> child erroring out with a '#608' message (since axiom-level annotations on non-Declaration axioms are uniformly deferred there), then a fixed-arity child check, then construct the Axiom variant with Vec::new() for its own (always-empty, pending #608) annotations field. Checked owl_functional_parser's DatatypeDefinition(...) parser as the cross-syntax precedent for the target Axiom::AxiomDatatypeDefinition(Vec<Annotation>, Datatype, DataRange) shape, and data_range.rs (#606) for the DataRange-parsing function to reuse rather than reimplement. Followed the repo's TDD workflow literally rather than writing tests and implementation in one pass: committed ignored unit tests (in a new datatype_definition.rs) plus ignored integration tests (owl_xml_parser/tests/owl_xml.rs) against a stub that unconditionally returns Err(...#694...), confirmed the crate built and the new tests showed as ignored, then unignored them and replaced the stub body with the real implementation (resolve_iri on the leading <Datatype> child, data_range() on the second child). No real design alternative existed here — the grammar maps directly onto an existing Axiom variant and an existing DataRange parser, so the only judgment call was matching existing conventions (annotation-rejection message wording, error-message style, module layout) rather than inventing new ones. Also updated docs/plans/OWL_XML_PLAN.md and the root CLAUDE.md owl_xml_parser paragraph to note #694 closed this slice of #608's original gap list, since #608 itself (ABox axioms, remaining annotation-axiom elements) stays open." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:722 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr722 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
